hi there steve kaufman here and today  i'm going to again talk about language  learning and if you like talking about  language learning please subscribe to my  channel  today i want to talk about  fitness and language learning and  particularly crossfit and language  learning now  we need to be fit in order to  engage in physical activity the more fit  we are normally the better we do in  sports for example in skiing or tennis  or whatever it might be and i think the  same is true in language learning uh we  need to make ourselves develop our our  stamina and our physical ability to  learn languages and this is something i  talked about in my japanese video and i  will get it be getting back to in that  japanese video  and in particular i want to talk about  crossfit because i started doing  crossfit here in vancouver ah a couple  of weeks ago and crossfit focuses on a  limited number of exercises they work  the legs the core and the shoulders but  always is sort of in a free-standing  situation you're doing squats you're  doing  jerks or snatches  and while it's controversial  their view is that this is very good  because you're not just focusing on one  muscle whereas if you're sitting at a  machine and i'm in a gym you might just  be working on your biceps or something  i have found it excellent i find that it  has improved my posture i feel very good  so  the question is is there sort of us a  limited number of exercises  that we can do in language learning that  you know by focusing on these we  increase our fitness fitness for  language learning now  remember that  uh whatever we whatever this sort of  concentrated exercise might be we still  have to do a number of other things  however  if we can increase our alertness our  ability to notice i think the ability to  notice is is like fitness in sports the  more things you notice the better you're  going to learn the language so what i've  been doing in the last week or so  uh is that i'll read my text in polish  and i'll focus on underlining and  highlighting more phrases and then i can  hear the text to speech  of those phrases so i kind of hear them  sounding in my mind often these are  phrases with verbs in them i think those  are the most important kinds of phrases  and then i go to the dictation section  at link and i hear the text to speech  and then i have to type in what i heard  dictation so i'm listening to two three  four five words of polish i have to  write in what i heard wow it's amazing  how i mishear how you assume you're  hearing something in fact what the  person said was quite different and so  training myself to hear better what is  said and to write correctly  uh is not only enabling me to remember  these phrases but is also increasing my  alertness my ability to notice therefore  my fitness so i think this  principle of crossfit like a limited  number of exercises that are very good  for you  it's not the only thing you do but they  really improve your general fitness i  think the same might be true of this  emphasis on phrases and then doing  dictation so but i'll continue doing  this and i'll report back to you but i  look forward to hearing your comments  thank you for listening bye for now  you
 

